<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal unemployed rose 1.2 pct mth/mth Nov - IFEP.</title>
<headline>Portugal unemployed rose 1.2 pct mth/mth Nov - IFEP.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of registered unemployed in Portugal rose 1.2 percent month-on-month in November to 462,511, up 3.5 percent year-on-year, the Institute for Employment and Professional Training (IFEP) said.</p>
<p>				    Nov 96   Oct 96    Nov 95</p>
<p> Registered unemployed	462,511  460,126  446,926</p>
<p> Percentage change (yr/yr)   +3.5 pct</p>
<p>Percentage change (mth/mth) +1.2 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - The IEFP does not express the number of unemployed as a percentage of the total labour force. Its figures for the number of people out of work are consistently higher than those of the National Statistics Institute (INE) -- the government's official yardstick for unemployment.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom 3511-3538254</p>
</text>
